Response: Thank you for this important comment. We have substantially clarified the experimental methodology and measurement scope to improve reproducibility. Specifically, we now explicitly define the operations included and excluded in each experiment. Trapdoor generation includes canonical-range decomposition and generation of all required context-bound ABSE tokens, while query processing includes all required ABSE  operations, authenticated bitmap reconstruction, and conjunctive bitmap evaluation. Aggregation, complete client-side verification, blockchain verification, and threshold decryption are measured separately. We have also clarified the throughput measurement scope and report statistical variability over 20 independent runs. These revisions align the reported measurements with the formal O(Nu,mc) search complexity and provide a clearer basis for interpreting and reproducing the performance results.

