Response: Thank you for this valuable suggestion. We agree that asymptotic communication complexity alone does not fully characterize the practical transmission overhead of BVCRSA. We have therefore added a numerical end-to-end communication evaluation using the actual serialized protocol objects. The measurement includes the complete two-round query exchange: query tokens and selected positions, authenticated protected bitmap blocks for all matched canonical nodes, all selected aggregation entries and their Merkle multi-proofs, and the two aggregate ciphertexts. The results are reported as actual transmitted bytes under varying query selectivities, thereby quantifying the growth associated with both authenticated bitmap transmission and the number of matched records and complementing the asymptotic analysis in TableV.

