Response: We sincerely thank the reviewer for the positive assessment of the revised manuscript and for recognizing the improvements to the bitmap key-provisioning mechanism, threat model, leakage characterization, security analysis, and experimental evaluation. We have carefully addressed the remaining suggestions as follows.
(1) Notation consistency: We performed a manuscript-wide consistency check and harmonized the notation used in the protocol description, security analysis, complexity analysis, and tables. In particular, symbols associated with query dimensions, canonical nodes, matched-node sets, query-derived position sets, aggregation ciphertexts, epoch states, and verification proofs are now used consistently throughout the manuscript.
(2) Blockchain cost: We agree that empirical blockchain overhead provides useful deployment insight. We have added a dedicated Blockchain Anchoring Overhead subsection reporting real measurements from a live 3-node Ethereum Clique-PoA consortium: gas consumption (43,829.80 +/- 3.69 gas/epoch), serialized transaction payload (124 +/- 0 bytes), and confirmation latency (5.877 +/- 0.438 s), mean +/- SD over 20 independent epoch submissions. We also show that this per-epoch cost is fixed-structure and therefore independent of dataset size N, while cumulative ledger storage instead scales with epoch-anchoring frequency. These results complement the existing blockchain-verification measurements and give a concrete, measured answer to the practical cost of blockchain anchoring rather than a conceptual one.
